{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.DilogPartBBranchPhase","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DilogPartBBranchPhase","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.DilogarithmArchimedeanLimit","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Complex.Log"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QPochhammer.clog_one_sub_pole_phase_split","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QPochhammer.clog_one_sub_pole_phase_split","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/DilogPartBBranchPhase.lean#L63-L78","doc":"**Part B — the exact per-factor pole + phase decomposition.**  Combining the\nbranch phase with the real algebraic split `log_neg_factor_split`, a negative\nfactor `1 − w` (`w = x qᵏ > 1`) decomposes into:\n\n`Log(1 − w) = log w + log(1 − w⁻¹) + iπ`,\n\ni.e. (i) the algebraic pole `log w` (linear-in-`k` divergence), (ii) the\nconvergent regularized piece `log(1 − w⁻¹)`, (iii) the branch-cut phase `iπ`.\nThis is exactly the per-factor object the Part-B pole-cancellation audit\nsubtracts (no free parameter). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QPochhammer.clog_one_sub_of_gt_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QPochhammer.clog_one_sub_of_gt_one","kind":"theorem","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/DilogPartBBranchPhase.lean#L40-L61","doc":"**Part B — the per-factor branch phase.**  For a negative real factor\n`1 − w` (`w > 1`), the principal complex logarithm picks up the `iπ`\nbranch phase on top of the real log-magnitude:\n\n`Log(1 − w) = log(w − 1) + iπ`.\n\nThis is the source of the branch-cut `iπ` tower in `(1−q)·log Φ_n` once\n`x qᵏ > 1` (i.e. `k > log_q(1/x)`), which the Part-A monotone-Riemann-sum\nargument does not see. ","signatureChunk":0}]}